/* book: lead: For an input that is not changing, a sensor is fully described by a small set of numbers. Each number answers a different question: how close to truth (accuracy), how repeatable (precision), how small a change it can see (resolution), how much output per input (sensitivity), how straight its graph is (linearity), and how it behaves going up versus down (hysteresis) or over time (drift). These are  */
