/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Range is the two limits the sensor is made for, such as 0–250 kPa or −40 to 125 °C.
   - S is sensitivity in output units per input unit (mV/kPa, mV/V per kPa, or counts/°C); Δy is a small output change; Δx is the input change that caused it.
   - For a straight sensor, S = output span / input span.
   - Accuracy is how close the mean indicated value is to the true value.
   - Resolution is the smallest input change that gives a detectable output change.
   - Linearity is the maximum deviation of the measured curve from a chosen straight line, as ± %FS.
   - L is linearity in %FS; ymeas is the measured output; yline is the chosen straight-line output at the same input; yspan is the full-scale output span.
   - Hysteresis is the maximum difference between up-scale and down-scale readings at the same input, expressed as %FS.
   - The figure draws the worked example.
*/
