/* book exam traps: Accuracy and precision are different. A sensor can be precise and still inaccurate by a fixed bias. | ± %FS and ± %reading differ hugely at low readings. 1 %FS on 0–250 kPa is ±2.5 kPa anywhere; 1 % of a 10 kPa reading is only ±0.1 kPa. | Resolution is not sensitivity. High sensitivity with poor resolution is possible. | Linearity without naming the straight line is incomplete. Terminal-based, best-fit and independent linearity give different numbers. | Hysteresis is up/down at the same input; drift is change with time or temperature. A zero shift after warming is drift, not hysteresis. */
